# AI Coding Rules for Glorium MedTech Test Automation Framework
# Targeted for: Cursor, Claude, GitHub Copilot

## General Principles
- Language: C# (.NET 8)
- Test Framework: NUnit 4.x with Microsoft.Playwright.NUnit
- Assertions: Playwright built-in Web Assertions (`Expect(locator).To...`) for UI, FluentAssertions for API/DTO verification
- Code Style: Clean Code, SOLID, idiomatic C# (file-scoped namespaces, nullable reference types, async/await everywhere)

## Architecture & Responsibilities
- `Glorium.Automation.Core`: Infrastructure only (config, browser context hooks, tracing, Bogus fake data generators).
- `Glorium.Automation.Api`: HTTP/REST clients (using Playwright `IAPIRequestContext` or HttpClient), DTOs, request builders. No UI logic.
- `Glorium.Automation.Ui`: Page Objects (`BasePage` subclasses) and Component Objects (`BaseComponent`). Never assert directly inside Page Objects (return locators or page states; keep assertions in test methods).
- `tests/*`: NUnit test fixtures. Keep tests readable as living documentation. Use Arrange-Act-Assert (AAA) pattern.

## Playwright Best Practices
- ALWAYS prefer user-facing locators:
  1. `GetByRole` (e.g. `Page.GetByRole(AriaRole.Button, new() { Name = "Submit" })`)
  2. `GetByLabel`, `GetByPlaceholder`, `GetByText`
  3. `GetByTestId` (configured to `data-testid`)
  4. Avoid brittle XPath or deep CSS chains (`div > div > span:nth-child(2)` is strictly forbidden).
- NEVER use `Thread.Sleep` or arbitrary `Task.Delay`. Rely on Playwright auto-waiting and `Expect(locator).ToBeVisibleAsync()`.
- Parallel safety: Tests must run in parallel without race conditions. Each test fixture or method must be isolated with unique data (use `MedicalDataFaker`).
- Tracing & Diagnostics: Attach Playwright Traces (`trace.zip`) on failure for post-mortem debugging.

## Healthcare / MedTech Domain Specifics
- Always mask or anonymize mock PHI (Protected Health Information) in logs.
- Generate valid formatted fake identifiers (e.g. US Insurance ID pattern, National Provider Identifier NPI, Equipment Serial numbers).
- Use Bogus `Faker` instances configured with `en_US` locale.

## Test Naming Convention
- Pattern: `[MethodOrFeature]_[Scenario]_[ExpectedResult]`
- Example: `CreateOrder_WithValidPatientAndEquipment_GeneratesPendingInvoice`
- Annotate with NUnit tags: `[Test, Category("E2E"), Category("Orders")]`
